  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1020 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nTemperatures will warm back up to seasonal norms by Wednesday, and\nthen continue to inch upward a little more by week's end. By\nThursday, we'll start to see heat indices in the low 100s in\nseveral areas west of the Cumberland Plateau, but it doesn't\nappear that we will quite reach Heat Advisory criteria at any\npoint in the 7-day forecast, so at least the risk of hazardous\nweather is very low for the foreseeable future. As far as expected\nrainfall amounts, total QPF values from today through Saturday \nnight range from a few hundredths of an inch along the Tennessee\nRiver to a little over 1\" across portions of the Cumberland\nPlateau. Even those higher amounts won't be excessive, but the\ngradient from west to east does show the wide range of rainfall\nprobabilities throughout the week with that pesky upper low \nwearing out its welcome.",
